How to Resolve Failed Cognos Schedules by Reassigning Credentials - Motio
Let’s say that Ed has configured many scheduled jobs and reports that go out to a number of people, but he has left the company. Shortly after Ed’s last day, several of these people are not receiving their scheduled Cognos reports.
That handy software I mentioned is MotioPI Pro, which provides a much simpler and faster way to manage this headache. The steps below show how to do it in MotioPI Pro.
Enter the credential property of the ex-employee in theValuetext area. In this example, we will enter Ed’s credential.
Then pressSubmitto issue the query to Cognos to find all scheduled items that match ex-employee Ed’s credentials.
Now that MotioPI Pro has located all of Ed’s schedules, use theChange Access Credentialsaction button to change the credentials of Ed’s schedules. 10.
11. In theSecurity Directory, expand the namespace and find the user’s name who will take over the schedules.
13. PressChange Credentialsto perform the action across all of Ed’s schedules.
