Have you ever wished you could recover the lost model based on information which is stored in your Cognos Content Store (e.g. a package which was published from the lost model)?
First – open up Framework Manager and create a new (empty) Framework Model. In the example shown below, we’ve called it “recover-lost-model”.
After you’ve launched MotioPI, go to the Model panel and click on the “Package Selector” button.
Select a package that was published from the Framework Model you’re trying to recover.
Click on the “save local” button to recover the model.xml file for the lost Framework Model.
Save the recovered model.xml file over the model.xml file which was created as part of the blank Framework Manager model in step 1.
