Fighting Zika With Data First, my experience.
But ultimately, the virus ran its course, infected a large portion of the population, and herd immunity developed, thus halting the spread. Today, Zika is considered endemic in some parts of the world with period breakouts.
For the coronavirus, it has been shown that some animals, like bats and deer , do carry the virus, but the main form of transmission is human-to-human.
So, let’s talk about vaccination/protection of high risk groups and herd immunity. Obviously, we’re far enough into this pandemic that public health officials and governments have already made these decisions and have decided a course of action.
Herd immunity is when a specific population reaches a percentage of individuals who are protected from the disease either by vaccine or through natural immunity. At that point, for those who are not immune, the risk of disease is low, because there are so few carriers.
Transmitted by blood transfusion, laboratory exposure 9
Likely airborne transmission 75
Perinatal diagnosis limited by sensitivity and specificity of ultrasound for detection of viral injury 20
Continued lack of testing capacity and laboratory reagents 42 Therapeutics Supportive care
Depending on the type of test administered, a positive result will either indicate that the patient has an active infection (rapid molecular PCR test or lab antigen tests) or has had an infection at some point (antibody test). If a person has symptoms consistent with COVID and a positive viral antigen test, action is warranted.
In dealing with Zika, public health recommendations include taking precautions at home that would prevent the incubation and growth of mosquitoes – eliminate standing water in your yard, remove potential reservoirs like old tires. Similarly, recommendations to reduce the spread of the coronavirus include physical distancing, masks and increased hygiene, like hand-washing and safe disposal of used tissues.
What we’ve learned is that it makes more sense to prioritize public health intervention to the most vulnerable and to populations at risk to the poorest medical outcomes. If we follow the economics, we have the data to justify dedicating more resources and control measures to:
Institutions which have people with underlying conditions which would contribute to adverse outcomes if they contracted coronavirus – hospitals, clinics
Case Counts of Zika in US and Territories
