As we welcome 2022 and the second half of the academic year, things result in surprises. This week there will be a better understanding of the sudden return of school closures in the USA.
At the beginning of December 2021, a new Covid-19 variant became discovered. This unknown and deadly variant became officially recognized in South Africa.
The effects are proven to be mild, yet still pose a large threat to global society. Furthermore, with the holiday season becoming observed, cases grow out of control and find their way to the USA.
Beginning of the End
To begin, as the winter holidays conclude for students in the USA, the time comes to return to their studies. Surprisingly, sudden emergency announcements are distributed to families and students from education institutes calling for a halt of in-person learning.
Meaning that teachers and other personnel are becoming victims to the wave of the Omicron variant. Indeed, these events prove to be a difficult period to adjust to as many parents are struggling to make sudden adjustments.
In turn, students’ patience, adaptability, and determination in the USA become challenged.
A child suffering from Covid-19 infection. One major initiation for schools shutting down in the USA.
As time goes forward and we reach the second anniversary of Covid-19 debuting to the world, things do not change. In this new chapter of variants, youths are becoming afflicted mentally and physically.
Moreover, this debatable topic becomes a subject for each school district to decide as cases vary from state. Nevertheless, this becomes a personal decision for the measures that are carried out by school officials.
Next, as schools begin to close during an unsteady spread of Covid-19, online learning platforms become predominant. This tool by now has not become foreign since computers and technology have provided great support for USA students.
Meaning that those in 9-12th grade levels earn the chance of graduating sooner than anticipated!
Followed by saving money and not commuting to campus. These are several things students can benefit from when it comes to the sudden closures of schools.
Furthermore, from some positive benefits present in students’ online learning platforms, comes another reason for the closures. Shortages of the Covid-19 test become scarcer as both small and large towns experience a rise in cases.
Despite this alarming rate, the state of New York distributes free tests for students to perform at home. The key attitude many are adopting is becoming vigilant and agile to combat this variant.
Besides the growth of resources becoming available to students during recent events of closures, there comes the mark on families. For certain, the Covid-19 pandemic has evolved the face of the workplace for many adults in the USA.
On the other hand, circumstances, where children study home alone, provide further concern for families. This situation becomes difficult to adjust to suddenly because many families are making sacrifices to make ends meet.
In all, the sudden effects of school closures in the USA range greatly.
Furthermore, households are coming to the point of overcoming sudden changes like school closures and having children restricted. These effects cause strain on many companies as most employed parents are forced to resign from their jobs.
Moreover, the fact of losing hands-on guidance, instruction, and interaction, things change once again with unexpected outlooks.
A young girl taking private study courses to further her education amidst school closures occurring in the USA. Image Source: (crhammlaw.com)
The Covid-19 pandemic that debuted nearly two years ago has provided one of the greatest challenges to adapt to. With this said, there are still ways to go when it comes to the evolution of education in the USA.
Another outlet to the changing face of education in the country can go to private studies becoming acknowledged. This and independent studies become popular as students can receive one-to-one interaction and receive the attention they need to succeed.
Besides the wheel of emotions and events plaguing schools in the USA, teachers and staff are working harder than ever. To illustrate, in Vermont, as the omicron variant ravages through communities, schools are experiencing shortages of instructors.
Without a doubt, these efforts become much appreciated but most campuses continue to experience temporary shutdowns. While most schools are required to have at least half of their population present to function, many resorts to this.
Furthermore, schools in the USA are also becoming adept at applying smart and proactive methods to avoid further delays. One example can be found in California where school districts in Oakland County are providing upgraded ventilation systems.
In other parts of the country like Maine, students are required to sit with plastic covers around their desks. Likewise, services in libraries also implement reduced service as certain books and study spaces require reservations in advance.
These actions are not only present in the state as it becomes witnessed in New York, California, and New Orléans. The reason for these events taking place derives from students not feeling safe and becoming overlooked despite obvious occurrences.
Another student illustrated “It feels like we are pawns”. Indeed, the lack of communication and proper care for students’ health sprouts to these events.
Most are becoming pushed to abandon their institutions and pursue independent studies. Nevertheless, the situation has evolved into a heated debate rooting back to shaping the education for schools in the USA.
Overall, many students will take various routes to meet their ends as education becomes disrupted with shutdowns owned by Omicron.
With students and families becoming overloaded with unnecessary burdens, stress, and danger, the face of education continues to develop.
