Jia Dashan said that from the perspective of demand, the global economy has continued to recover since the beginning of this year, and international trade has quickly resumed growth. Compared with the same period in 2019, the demand for container transportation has increased by about 6%.
The continuous shortage of crew supply has also increased the shortage. The complicated epidemic situation in major seafarer countries such as the Philippines and India, coupled with crew shifts and isolation, has led to a continuous increase in crew costs in the maritime market.
