Can shut-off valves and gate valves be mixed?
Structure When the installation space is limited, please pay attention to the selection:
From the appearance point of view, the gate valve is taller than the shut-off valve and the shut-off valve is longer than the gate valve in the case of the same caliber. In addition, the gate valve can be divided into bright rod and dark rod.
The flow rate is different, the gate valve is required to be fully open or fully closed, but the stop valve is not required. The shut-off valve has specified inlet and outlet directions, and the gate valve has no inlet and outlet direction requirements.
The shut-off valve can be used for cut-off and flow adjustment. The fluid resistance of the globe valve is relatively large, and it is more laborious to open and close, but because the distance between the valve plate and the sealing surface is short, the opening and closing stroke is short.
From the perspective of flow resistance, the flow resistance of the gate valve is small when fully opened, and the flow resistance of the load stop valve is large. The flow resistance coefficient of ordinary gate valve is about 0.08~0.12, the opening and closing force is small, and the medium can flow in two directions.
When the shut-off valve is installed, the medium can enter from below the valve core and enter from above in two ways.
The disadvantage of the medium entering from the bottom of the valve core is that the driving torque of the valve is relatively large, about 1.05~1.08 times that of the above entering, the valve stem is subjected to large axial force, and the valve stem is easy to bend. For this reason, the way that the medium enters from below is generally only suitable for small-diameter stop valves (below DN50).
The disadvantage of the way the medium enters from above is just the opposite of the way the medium enters from below. In fact, it can flow in both directions, just considering different perspectives.
