Causes of problems in the injection molding process of PVC pipe fittings
Injection molding pipe fittings often encounter the phenomenon that the mold cannot be filled in the process of processing. When the injection molding machine just started working, because the mold temperature was too low, the heat loss of the molten PVC material was large, which was prone to early solidification, and the resistance of the mold cavity was large, and the material could not fill the cavity.
If the gate is too small or the flow channel section is too small, the material flow resistance is too large. The gate and runner section can be enlarged to reduce melt flow resistance.
The formula is unreasonable, so that the plasticization of the material is not in place or the filler is too much, the formula should be adjusted, and the plasticization quality and fluidity of the material should be improved through the reasonable combination of processing aids, and the amount of fillers should be controlled. Insufficient mold cooling, improve mold cooling effect.
The temperature of the melted material is low, and the heating temperature of the barrel can be appropriately increased, especially the nozzle temperature should be increased. If the injection pressure or injection speed is low, the injection pressure or injection speed can be appropriately increased.
The set cooling time is not enough, you can increase the cooling time appropriately. If the amount of sol is insufficient, increase the amount of sol appropriately.
