Principle of microbial strain technology for sewage treatment News
Microbial treatment of sewagemainly removes organic pollutants (BOD, COD substances) in colloidal and dissolved state in sewage, and the removal rate can reach more than 90%, so that organic pollutants can meet the discharge standard.
Microbial treatment Sewage can be divided into aerobic treatment system and anaerobic treatment system according to the state of oxygen in the treatment process.
The primary treatment process is: the raw sewage that has passed through the coarse grid is lifted by the sewage lift pump - passed through the grid or sieve - and then enters the grit chamber - the sewage separated by the sand and water enters the primary sedimentation tank, the above is: Primary processing (ie physical processing). The function of the grit chamber is to remove inorganic particles with a large specific gravity.
to eutrophication of water body. The methods used include biological denitrification and phosphorus removal, coagulation sedimentation, sand rate method, activated carbon adsorption method, ion exchange method and electroosmosis analysis method.
