Battambang - Cambodia
Cycle developing basic skills and knowledge CE2, CM1 , CM2 | French International School of Battambang
All other students begin classes on Monday 3rd September 2018 at 8:00
Linguistic diversity and cultural diversity on the agenda!
The Ecole Française de Battambang is an International French School in Battambang Cambodia, which started in October 2012. The school is international and welcomes children from various nationalities.
In addition to the regular classes, EFB organizes optional extra-curricular activities. These activities are open in priority to EFB students and, if space allows, to other children of the community.
Parents are invited to lead extra-curricular activities in their areas of expertise.
The EFB works closely and effectively with the Embassy of France in Cambodia and with the French Institute of Cambodia (IFC), both in Phnom Penh and Battambang, where children can go to the IFC library to read and take out books.
YOUNG PROFESSIONAL PHOTOGRAPHERS!
If there are enough secondary school students (11 to 15 years old) wishing to continue their studies at the EFB, a class can be started using theCNEDas teaching tool.
EFB proposes the following optional extracurricular activities, available depending on the number of interested students: Khmer, English, Chinese, music (piano, violin), art. Activities can be developed and offered based on parents’ interest and support.
The school makes available a refrigerator where children can store their lunch and drinks. All containers must be clearly marked with the student’s name.
Parents volunteer to watch and help the children during the luch break. The cost of this activity for the school year 2015-2016 is USD 1 per week for children eating once or twice a week and USD 2 per week for children eating three or four times per week.
IN ONE PAYMENT AT THE BEGINNING OF THE SCHOOL YEAR,
TWO OR MORE CHILDREN REGISTERED BY A FAMILY:
IN ONE INSTALLMENT AT THE BEGINNING OF THE SCHOOL YEAR
H. CNED: FOR PARENTS OF CHILDREN REGISTERED WITH CNED, ALL EXPENSES RELATED TO THE CNED AND BILLED BY THE CNED MUST BE PAID DIRECTLY TO CNED. ALL LOCAL EXPENSES RELATED TO CNED MUST BE PAID BY THE PARENTS OR REIMBURSED TO EFB (including cost of posting homework)
EFB also supports development activities in the education sector in Battambang: training of Cambodian early childhood educators in Montessori techniques and a scholarship programme for children of underprivileged Cambodian families.
For the primary and secondary cycle, the teachers will provide a list of school supplies to be purchased by the parents before the start of the school year. Teachers may occasionally request some additional supplies, as required, during the school year.
In addition to the regular classes, EFB organizes optional extra-curricular activities. These activities are open in priority to students of EFB and, if space allows, to other children in the community.
