Intercropping of chilies (or other short-term crops) between young orange trees is a type of agro-forestry system which increases income, makes ultimate use of land resources, saves time for maintenance and irrigation, and improves soil fertility by using crop residue with cow manure as fertilizer, thereby reducing the use of chemicals.
Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology (2015)
The benefits of this kind of agroforestry are permanent soil cover, less soil degradation, optimal light and shadow situation and microclimate (different high of plants), better organic matter maintenance (decomposition of leaves and pruning residuals), better control of pests and diseases though higher amount beneficial insect species what led finally to high crop quality.
The farmer is able to generate income continuously from the short-term crops before the long-term crop provides its yield.
If the farmer plants only orange trees, the time consume for maintenance will be similar to the time consume for maintenance of both, orange trees and chilies, thus, this practice saves time in crop maintenance.
This technique can maintain the soil’s moisture and does not lead to soil compaction because the soil obtains additional fertilizer and especially organic waste.
Cow manure, chicken manure, rice husk, botanical pesticides has to be bought. Digging the pond and buying the water pumping machine are the most important factors affecting the costs.
Watering (Timing/ frequency: Two times per day or three times per day depend on the weather.)
Due to the permanent soil cover, the high crop diversification and the sophisticated pest control the risk of production failure decreased.
The crop diversification requires a lot of monetary inputs mainly for the establishment and also for the maintenance (labor for digging the pond, water pumping machine, natural fertilizers has to be bought - she does not raise animals). farm income
Although the land user had to invest a lot of money for this technology, she got and get still better and regular daily income from the sale of the wide range of different crops at the market compared to what she earned before. All in all she was able to improve the household's livelihood.
Due to the improved soil cover by the different vegetables and herbs all year long the evaporation deceased.
All year long the soil is covered by different vegetables and herbs.
The soil life increased regarding bacteria and fungi, earthworm, ant, and centipede due to the crop rotation system and the use of natural fertilizers and botanical pesticides.
The pest and disease control is improved due to the rotational system, the use of botanical pesticides, and the cultivation of companion plants such as anise basil, Cambodian mint and spring onions.
