Create a strong fanbase on other platforms
If you create a large following on YouTube, you can funnel them to your Twitch channel. YouTube is also very competitive, but with proper keyword research, good editing, a strong thumbnail, and a good title, you can start to grow your YouTube audience.
Engage with your viewers
There could be times when a particular game is saturated with other streamers, making it difficult for a small streamer to get noticed. For example, if you are looking to gain new viewers, the worst time to stream is perhaps during a holiday.
The truth is, most of these streamers are playing the same games and offering the same content as the others.
If you want Twitch to become a strong income source for you, you need to treat your channel like a business. That means your streams are your products and your viewers are your customers.
If you want to foster your streaming community, having your Discord server is a great way to do so. The best thing about Discord is that you can interact with your viewers while streaming, and even when you are not.
However, great content can do nothing if there is no one to watch it. If you are new to Twitch and want to increase your following, you should pay for viewers.
