We see this issue as building upon these field-shifting perspectives and utilizing specifically The Peer Review’s platform as a multimodal, open-access, and sustainable forum for disseminating scholarly inquiry and restoring justice. This is a theme that necessarily invites critique: What does it mean to enact “restorative justice”?
How has justice been shaped institutionally and historically, and how might we shape it differently?
