Primer: Put the main agent and hardener of the material in proportion, mix it fully with a mixer, and evenly coat the material with a brush, roller brush or spray gun when in use to form a primer paint, and the paint loading time is separated More than 8 hours.
Intermediate coating: Take a quantitative ratio of the main agent and hardener, stir it evenly with a mixer, then put in the quartz aggregate, stir evenly, use a trowel to flatten the above mixture on top of the primer within the usable time , So that the cavities and pinholes are filled.
The main purpose of polishing is to increase the brightness of the stone surface. Stone polishing is generally carried out according to the procedure of rough grinding → semi-fine grinding → fine grinding → fine grinding → polishing, and some of the rough grinding steps can be omitted, mainly depending on whether the surface of the original stone has undergone preliminary treatment.
②Semi-fine grinding: remove the traces of rough grinding to form new finer lines, so that the surface of the stone is smooth and smooth;
④Fine grinding: The surface of the stone after the precision grinding, without any traces of naked eyes. The surface is getting smoother, and the gloss can reach up to 55 degrees or more;
