News - The European Renaissance is inseparable from the technical support of Chinese papermaking and printing
China invented paper for daily use as early as the Eastern Han Dynasty. With the promotion of technology and the development of science and technology, block printing gained a large-scale popularization in the Tang Dynasty, and movable type printing was also invented by Bi Sheng during the Northern Song Dynasty—This is well known.
The Liberation Movement of Mind: The Renaissance. Chinese papermaking and printing, as a kind of production promotion technology in the cultural field, undoubtedly the most intuitive influence must be concentrated in the field of culture and art, but culture and political economy will interact again-so to say, Chinese papermaking and printing The connection with the European Renaissance is much closer than we think.
Chinese papermaking and printing were hundreds of years earlier than Western printing, and it was just as the European Renaissance was in full swing. China’s papermaking technology supplemented with improved printing technology can be said to be a “golden combination” in the field of cultural communication.
Not only that, papermaking and printing began to permeate all aspects of social life, and cultural communication has gradually evolved from the previous basic sensory communication to a culture that uses reading and writing as an interactive method. Moreover, because the driving factors of the papermaking and printing industries began to be determined gradually by demand and profit, rather than by the so-called authority before the Renaissance—religious orthodoxy or political ideology.
Because of the introduction of the two technologies, the economic consumption of cultural products has been greatly reduced, and the ability to buy books has become an economic goal that is relatively easy for the general public to achieve. The speed and quantity of book distribution indicate that cultural dissemination can already be made through Chinese papermaking and printing.
Printing and publishing organizations not only print texts, but the revolutionary impact of printing also includes dazzling printed images. This has a huge impact on the ignorant, especially when these images are used for the propaganda purpose of Renaissance thought.
To this extent, the modern Chinese printing technology of movable type printing and large-scale industrial printing after development has actually benefited from European innovation and technological advancement. Secondly, the literary review also enabled the European continent to learn about ancient technologies from the far east, spread the wisdom of ancient Chinese people, and expanded the influence of Chinese culture and technology.
And with the advancement of the Renaissance, the publishing content of the publishing industry began to be enriched, which has increasingly promoted the development of Chinese papermaking and printing, and its development has also expanded the scope of the Renaissance’s spread and broadened its influence. level.
Before the Renaissance, that is, around the middle of the Middle Ages in Europe, the development of social sciences was very slow, and the general education of mathematics, physics and chemistry was popularized to a wider social class. It was after the Renaissance that it got significant development.
In addition, Chinese papermaking and printing have also accelerated the emergence of the core ideas of the Renaissance, awakened people’s pursuit of real life, and firstly consolidated the stable position of the bourgeoisie on the ideological level, thereby benefiting the development of cities and the future. The germination of capitalism even promoted the theoretical system that formed the capitalist system to some extent.
Papermaking has made the media portable and relatively cheap, allowing more people to have access to writing, and thus have literacy capabilities; the production and popularization of printing has made it possible for the production and dissemination of knowledge for the public, and further promoted the popularization of knowledge. Cultivated and prepared a knowledgeable labor force for the industrial revolution at the end of the eighteenth century.
And because of the success of ideological changes, new classes were born, which not only promoted the process of European capitalism, but also developed social civilization. On the other hand, due to the continuous expansion of literate population, people’s demand for information and the richness of demand have greatly increased, which has promoted information production and innovation.
From these points, the European Renaissance undoubtedly did it. Since the introduction of Chinese papermaking and printing as a booster of the Renaissance to Europe, it has not only promoted the Renaissance in the West, but also greatly reduced the cost of books, making knowledge popular, and the prosperity of Western technology and culture began.
