Printing a book is not easy, this article will take you to understand the post-printing process SmartFortune printing
Hot stamping and silver hot stamping: Hot stamping of metal foil (gold and silver foil) on the surface of the printed product using hot pad printing, so that the surface of the product has a metallic texture and effect.
Embossing: The embossing process is a process that uses a concave-convex mold to produce plastic deformation of the printed matter under a certain pressure, thereby performing artistic processing on the surface of the printed matter. After embossing, the surface of the printed matter presents patterns and textures of different depths, with obvious embossed three-dimensional effect, which enhances the artistic appeal of the printed matter
Forming process Die-cutting: The die-cutting process is to make a special die-cutting knife according to the design requirements of the printed matter, and then roll-cut the printed matter or other substrates into the desired shape or cut under pressure.
Indentation: If the paper is too thick, or the printed product with too brittle pulp is directly folded, the inner pulp is exposed, causing serious damage to the picture. Indentation is a good way to solve this problem.
Locking glue binding: Locking glue binding avoids the shortcomings of wireless glue binding that it is easy to loose pages and degumming. It is often used in book binding with more pages, such as dictionary books.
When binding, each signature is threaded first and then glued, and there is no milling when glueing. The book bound by this binding method is strong and flat, and currently there are more books using this method.
