A process of making hardcover books with a single machine and by hand. The process is divided into three lines, namely book block, book cover and sleeve.
The process is divided into three lines
Book block processing flow: start of semi-finished printed sheet → bumping → cutting → gluing and sleeve pages → gluing ring lining → collating → sewing → semi-finished product inspection → flattening → stacking and flattening → cutting book → binding book → applying adhesive~ →Dry separate book→Cut book→
Book seal processing process: Calculate the size of each material of the book shell → open material → apply adhesive → shell assembly → shell plug corner → flattening → natural drying → hot stamping.
