The following are some of the drawbacks to using asphalt shingle roofing for your home:
Asphalt shingles can crack– Because of how light they are, asphalt shingles can crack more easily, especially when they are exposed to extreme temperature fluctuations. Extreme temperature fluctuations can cause shingles to expand and contract, resulting in cracks.
This can cause the shingles to become damaged during installation. Asphalt shingles don’t offer a unique look– Although they won’t damage the curb appeal of your home with their look, asphalt shingles aren’t exactly unique.
These are some of the pros and cons of using asphalt shingles. Be sure to keep these pros and cons in mind when comparing the use of asphalt shingles to other options and to help make your decision.
